# The image must be built from sources only. Without these exclusions a checkout that has
# node_modules/ or .next/ present ships host artefacts into the build context — foreign-
# platform binaries break `pnpm install --frozen-lockfile`, and the context balloons to
# hundreds of MB. `.env*` is excluded even though the Dockerfile does not COPY it, so a
# future `COPY .` can never leak credentials into an image.
.git
.gitignore
**/node_modules
**/.next
**/dist
**/coverage
**/*.tsbuildinfo
**/*.tgz
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
tmp
.storage
.toolchain
.pnpm-store
.vite
.vite-temp
.DS_Store
core
